# EME platform

Multi-vendor commerce with Reels and Live Shopping. Build on this foundation only.

## Stack

- Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript ES modules. No framework, no bundler, no Node backend.
- Supabase for Auth, Postgres, RLS, Storage, Realtime, and Edge Functions.
- LiveKit for live video only.
- Load Supabase JS v2 from `https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2` inside `assets/js/core/supabase-client.js`.

## Layout

- `index.html` and `pages/` are routes. Pages share the head, anti-flash theme script, and shell.
- `assets/css/` is tokens, base, components, layout, utilities — in that order.
- `assets/js/core/` is config, client, state, theme, and icons.
- `assets/js/components/` is shared UI (shell, toast, modal, dropdown, skeleton).
- `assets/js/modules/` is feature code. Keep modules small.
- `supabase/` is backend SQL, policies, and Edge Functions. Do not invent a second backend.

## CSS

Always use variables from `assets/css/tokens.css`. Never hardcode colors in component or layout CSS.

```css
/* BAD */
color: #6D5DFC;
/* GOOD */
color: var(--color-primary);
```

The inline theme script may set only `#F8F9FC` and `#0B0B12` so the first paint matches `--color-bg`. Reels and Live stay dark via `body[data-page="reels|live"]`.

## Data

- All Supabase calls go through `assets/js/core/supabase-client.js`.
- RLS is the security layer. Never trust the frontend for authorization.
- `config.js` holds the project URL and anon key only. Never put a `service_role` key in frontend code, HTML, or git.

## JavaScript

- ES modules and small functions. One job per file.
- JSDoc on exported functions.
- No business rules inside shell or design-system components.
- Icons come from `assets/js/core/icons.js`. Do not use emoji as icons.
